cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "FlashProve-Next: Verifiable Inference for Production LLM APIs"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/s-JoL/FlashProve-Next"
url: "https://s-jol.github.io/FlashProve-Next/"
authors:
  - family-names: Song
    given-names: Liang
    email: sl12160010@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  Publicly verifiable zero-knowledge proofs for closed-weight language-model APIs under unchanged
  native floating-point production serving (bf16/fp8, random sampling, FlashAttention, CUDA Graphs,
  continuous batching, prefix caching) while keeping weights, architecture, hidden system prompts,
  hidden chain of thought, and multi-turn state private. Includes ten formal protocol specifications,
  19 machine-checked Lean 4.29.1 modules (219 declarations, zero sorry), GPU certified-tolerance
  calibration across 392,928 blocks, an out-of-core streaming F_{p^3} prover (1.51 B/cell) and
  standalone CPU verifier demonstrated on unsliced Qwen3-0.6B with live vLLM 0.33, and offline
  laptop verification bundles.
keywords:
  - verifiable inference
  - zero-knowledge proofs
  - LLM serving
  - cryptography
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
